From 36b5038192ee9e5375e854e45d7061a2fffcb1df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cwriter <cwriter@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sycl : ESIMD grouped MoE GEMM for the 8x8x16 sub-group-8 XMX
 shape (Xe-HPG)

The register-operand ESIMD grouped GEMM only stood in for the 8x16x16
sub-group-16 joint_matrix combination, so Arc A-series (Xe-HPG) and
ARL-H, whose XMX shape is 8x8x16 on sub-group 8, kept the SLM-staging
joint_matrix kernel and saw no change.

Template the kernel on a gg_arch: the dpas width NW, the rows of one
thread and whether 2D block loads exist.
- Xe2 / Xe-HPC: 16 wide, 32 rows, 2D loads, as before.
- Xe-HPG: 8 wide, 16 rows, 1D loads. It has 256 registers of 32 bytes,
  half of Xe2's file, so 32-row accumulators alone would take half of
  it, and it has no 2D block messages: B is read one 1D block load per
  packed row, and the reordered A through the gather path the canonical
  layout already used.
The format decoders take the row count and the slice type as template
parameters; the arithmetic is unchanged. fg_esimd_combo and the remap
take the 8x8x16 sub-group-8 f16/bf16 combinations, FG_AOT_SG moves to
fused-gemm.hpp, and an AOT build compiles only the kernels of its width.

A test build (GGML_SYCL_GG_ESIMD_EMULATE_DPAS8) computes the 8-wide dpas
in software, so the Xe-HPG kernel runs on an Xe2 device with
GGML_SYCL_MMID_ESIMD_XEHPG=1. That software dpas matches the hardware
16-wide dpas to an NMSE of 5e-15 (f16) and 4e-16 (bf16).

Checked on Arc Pro B60 (no Xe-HPG hardware was available):
- test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT_ID: 1152/1152 for the Xe-HPG kernel
  (software dpas) and for the Xe2 kernels, GGML_SYCL_MMID_ESIMD 1 and
  2, f16 and bf16; shifting the Xe-HPG B tiles by one fails 174 cases
- acm-g10 AOT: all 40 default-mode Xe-HPG kernels take 256 registers
  with no spill, 8-wide dpas only and no 2D block message
- bmg-g21 AOT: the 40 default-mode Xe2 kernels match the previous
  ones in instruction count, register allocation, dpas and sends
- llama-bench prefill, Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M and UD-IQ3_XXS, one B60:
  within 0.15% of before (pp512/pp2048)

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
